WEBVTT

00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:15.100
Why are you in my room?

00:00:18.530 --> 00:00:20.000
Oh,

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:22.660
I didn't know you had such a deep reason to be here.

00:00:23.080 --> 00:00:24.160
Really?

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:30.840
Don't come near me!

00:00:44.230 --> 00:00:45.560
Seriously,

00:00:45.560 --> 00:00:48.000
go back to space if you're really an alien.

00:00:50.450 --> 00:00:53.380
No one's here to take you back? They ditched you?

00:00:57.500 --> 00:01:00.200
Can aliens live without oxygen?

00:01:03.090 --> 00:01:04.360
Recession, huh?

00:01:08.060 --> 00:01:10.510
Why do all aliens love Earth?

00:01:12.330 --> 00:01:15.390
Oh? Then go to a country where there's a lot of hotties.

00:01:17.330 --> 00:01:21.100
Man, this girl is really annoying.

00:03:01.450 --> 00:03:03.160
What are your hobbies?

00:03:03.160 --> 00:03:07.080
I'm not really sure if this counts, but I'm into deep sea creatures.

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:09.870
Like deep sea fish, shrimp, and crab?

00:03:09.870 --> 00:03:10.670
That's right.

00:03:11.580 --> 00:03:15.170
I can't help but feel intrigued by the deep sea.

00:03:15.170 --> 00:03:21.430
It's mysterious, but far more within our reach than outer space.

00:03:21.430 --> 00:03:23.090
Any cute ones?

00:03:23.090 --> 00:03:26.220
You know, the kind that makes you want to fish them right up!

00:03:26.220 --> 00:03:27.680
Some are cute in a gross way.

00:03:28.020 --> 00:03:30.060
Hmm... gross?

00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:31.890
At least pick up on the cute part.

00:03:35.860 --> 00:03:39.690
With the seating change, I lost the chance to finish my conversation with Maekawa-san.

00:03:39.690 --> 00:03:42.410
I'm far away from Ryuushi-san too.

00:03:42.410 --> 00:03:48.240
But she does walk over to my desk to have lunch with me.

00:03:48.830 --> 00:03:52.330
My school life is gearing up nicely.

00:03:52.330 --> 00:03:55.290
I consider it to be like the front wheel of a bicycle.

00:03:55.290 --> 00:03:59.420
The problem lies in my home life, the rear wheel.

00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:05.970
We go on a bike ride once every three days, but she takes a walk on other days...

00:04:05.970 --> 00:04:11.350
to the sea where she lost her memory, looking for traces of aliens.

00:04:12.190 --> 00:04:15.610
Is it so terrifying to have no memory?

00:04:15.610 --> 00:04:17.230
It must be.

00:04:17.900 --> 00:04:21.240
Your former self might as well be dead.

00:04:26.490 --> 00:04:30.240
Sometimes, we run into the cosplaying Maekawa-san at night.

00:04:30.240 --> 00:04:32.620
Erio always goes home ahead of me when we do.

00:04:34.210 --> 00:04:36.750
What's your opinion on the existence of aliens?

00:04:36.750 --> 00:04:38.790
Aliens?

00:04:38.790 --> 00:04:40.380
Did you get infected by the Touwa virus?

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:43.340
No, I'm simply curious.

00:04:43.340 --> 00:04:44.510
Let's see.

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:47.510
It doesn't seem much different from religion.

00:04:47.510 --> 00:04:50.930
Some people believe in them and feel comforted by it.

00:04:50.930 --> 00:04:56.520
They both involve looking for reassurance in something that can't be seen.

00:04:58.150 --> 00:04:59.020
I see.

00:04:59.570 --> 00:05:01.650
Is this really not about Touwa?

00:05:02.320 --> 00:05:03.570
Maybe just a bit.

00:05:08.450 --> 00:05:13.250
I'm meeting her on a day off because she wanted to show me around the city.

00:05:13.750 --> 00:05:15.790
Morning!

00:05:15.790 --> 00:05:16.960
It's so hot!

00:05:16.960 --> 00:05:19.340
Yo! Uh...

00:05:19.340 --> 00:05:20.670
That's pretty stylish.

00:05:20.670 --> 00:05:24.550
Oh, this? Sorry, my morning practice dragged on.

00:05:24.550 --> 00:05:26.550
I didn't have the time to change.

00:05:26.550 --> 00:05:29.140
It's really embarrassing, but I didn't want to make you wait.

00:05:29.140 --> 00:05:32.220
I don't mind it.
Where's your bike?

00:05:33.310 --> 00:05:34.310
I ran here.

00:05:34.310 --> 00:05:35.140
Why?

00:05:35.140 --> 00:05:37.440
I have to wear my helmet when I ride.

00:05:37.440 --> 00:05:39.110
Oh, right.

00:05:39.110 --> 00:05:42.780
It would've squished my hair, so I ended up running.

00:05:43.110 --> 00:05:45.400
You crazy girl!

00:05:46.280 --> 00:05:49.870
Oh! Lucky me, I'm going faster than walking pace!

00:05:49.870 --> 00:05:52.660
Niwa-kun, you're not making sense!

00:05:52.660 --> 00:05:54.290
Whoa, you're a circus performer!

00:05:55.160 --> 00:05:56.540
Niwa-sama, table for two.

00:05:56.540 --> 00:05:59.790
Yes! I'm pumped pumped up up!

00:06:00.840 --> 00:06:02.590
This is truly calcium-color.

00:06:02.590 --> 00:06:07.050
It doesn't seem to be popular with kids, so I'll mix in some carrot juice!

00:06:13.720 --> 00:06:16.600
The prototype is ready. Drink up!

00:06:16.600 --> 00:06:17.850
Me?

00:06:17.850 --> 00:06:18.600
It'll be great.

00:06:18.600 --> 00:06:19.850
Here I go.

00:06:21.560 --> 00:06:22.690
It wasn't sweet enough?

00:06:23.190 --> 00:06:24.980
I can't drink carbonated stuff.

00:06:25.690 --> 00:06:29.070
Sorry! You should've told me.

00:06:29.070 --> 00:06:32.870
But failure is the mother of success!

00:06:32.870 --> 00:06:37.120
This means no one is born unless mothers make mistakes.

00:06:40.250 --> 00:06:44.550
All right, I'll get you to shoot beams out of your mouth this time!

00:06:44.550 --> 00:06:46.420
When are you going to finish that drink of yours?

00:06:46.420 --> 00:06:49.840
A father is needed for success too.

00:06:49.840 --> 00:06:52.800
A happily-married couple!

00:06:57.310 --> 00:06:59.440
Ryuushi-san, do you have any special talents?

00:06:59.440 --> 00:07:01.350
It's Ryuuko!

00:07:01.350 --> 00:07:03.360
Special talents, huh?

00:07:03.360 --> 00:07:05.020
10 yen coins... no.

00:07:05.020 --> 00:07:06.900
Rope... no.

00:07:06.900 --> 00:07:10.400
Sometimes I can use child tickets for... That's dumb...

00:07:11.410 --> 00:07:12.780
I don't have any.

00:07:12.780 --> 00:07:14.330
No, wait, I do!

00:07:14.330 --> 00:07:15.330
You didn't hear that.

00:07:15.330 --> 00:07:16.700
Boomska boom boom!

00:07:17.080 --> 00:07:18.580
If you don't have any...

00:07:18.580 --> 00:07:21.330
Blasters! I mean, blasphemy!

00:07:21.330 --> 00:07:23.210
I have special talents, tons of them!

00:07:24.130 --> 00:07:25.090
Oh, I know!

00:07:25.090 --> 00:07:31.050
My elementary school teacher said I was the best at growing cyclamen flowers in class!

00:07:31.050 --> 00:07:34.180
So, you were spreading lots of flower <i>particles</i>.

00:07:34.180 --> 00:07:38.100
Although, I cheated by planting hyacinths.

00:07:38.100 --> 00:07:39.560
Here you go.

00:07:42.770 --> 00:07:44.270
May I ask you something else?

00:07:44.270 --> 00:07:45.770
Sure, fire away.

00:07:45.770 --> 00:07:47.530
Ryuushi-san,

00:07:48.030 --> 00:07:49.400
what do you consider to be mystical?

00:07:53.280 --> 00:07:56.410
Hold on, I'll use the serious side of my brain.

00:07:59.290 --> 00:08:00.410
Let's see...

00:08:00.410 --> 00:08:01.790
I have the answer!

00:08:01.790 --> 00:08:02.670
Yes?

00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:04.290
It's doing this!

00:08:04.290 --> 00:08:05.170
Thank you for waiting.

00:08:05.670 --> 00:08:07.590
Tomato salad for two.

00:08:07.590 --> 00:08:08.880
Both hers.

00:08:10.630 --> 00:08:12.340
Enjoy your stay.

00:08:16.850 --> 00:08:20.390
You really creeped out the waitress with that one.

00:08:20.390 --> 00:08:23.190
It's not about that. There's more to it!

00:08:24.850 --> 00:08:28.730
Seeing things, hearing things, and saying things...

00:08:29.110 --> 00:08:31.490
Everything is mystical to me.

00:08:31.490 --> 00:08:34.110
We learn the basics in biology class,

00:08:34.110 --> 00:08:36.740
but to be honest, I don't really get it.

00:08:36.740 --> 00:08:41.750
The same goes for things we use every day, like how phones work.

00:08:42.160 --> 00:08:44.750
I don't know why cycling is faster than walking either.

00:08:44.750 --> 00:08:48.880
Doesn't that make you wonder how many things you actually <i>do</i> know?

00:08:48.880 --> 00:08:49.750
But...

00:08:50.210 --> 00:08:51.880
But somehow I'm still alive.

00:08:53.130 --> 00:08:57.140
It makes me think there's a labyrinth of mysteries that's keeping me alive.

00:08:57.470 --> 00:08:59.890
That's what I ponder sometimes before going to sleep.

00:09:01.520 --> 00:09:02.640
You're right!

00:09:03.520 --> 00:09:07.900
Geez, it's embarrassing that I'm so dumb.

00:09:07.900 --> 00:09:09.610
You pass, Ryuushi-san!

00:09:09.610 --> 00:09:12.400
What? I pass? Yay!

00:09:12.400 --> 00:09:15.910
After that, she took me around many places near the station.

00:09:15.910 --> 00:09:19.120
It was a very fulfilling way to spend a day off.

00:09:20.370 --> 00:09:21.830
See ya!

00:09:29.540 --> 00:09:30.380
Look what we have here.

00:09:35.170 --> 00:09:36.470
Want a ride?

00:09:36.470 --> 00:09:37.840
Or would you rather pedal?

00:09:37.840 --> 00:09:42.260
It is humiliating to operate a primitive tool designed for weak bodies like the cousin's.

00:09:42.260 --> 00:09:43.890
Actually, why don't you just fly?

00:09:43.890 --> 00:09:45.770
It's easier than walking.

00:09:45.770 --> 00:09:47.020
Well, I guess you can't fly

00:09:47.020 --> 00:09:48.600
even though you're an alien.

00:09:49.480 --> 00:09:52.980
You'll just fall into a river with your bike again.

00:09:53.730 --> 00:09:57.360
You want to believe your lost memories are stored somewhere, right?

00:09:57.360 --> 00:10:01.370
That there must be aliens, and it's in their hands.

00:10:01.370 --> 00:10:03.490
But you couldn't fly.

00:10:03.490 --> 00:10:05.370
You aren't even an alien.

00:10:05.830 --> 00:10:07.410
Isn't that why you wrapped a futon around yourself?

00:10:07.410 --> 00:10:09.710
To tell yourself that you can't fly because you can't ride a bike wearing that.

00:10:12.130 --> 00:10:15.760
Hanging by a thread of an excuse...

00:10:15.760 --> 00:10:17.800
I can't blame her for that.

00:10:17.800 --> 00:10:22.640
I just find it disturbing she's using aliens as the excuse.

00:10:23.850 --> 00:10:26.020
You're not going to give me a long explanation?

00:10:26.020 --> 00:10:29.520
I have no intention of talking to feeble-minded humanoids.

00:10:29.520 --> 00:10:30.730
Fine.

00:10:34.650 --> 00:10:38.070
Let's play, Mako-chan!

00:10:38.070 --> 00:10:40.030
Act your age.

00:10:40.030 --> 00:10:43.030
Why? You're still a kid.

00:10:43.030 --> 00:10:44.160
It's not about me!

00:10:45.410 --> 00:10:47.620
Hmm... deep sea creatures.

00:10:47.620 --> 00:10:49.370
Why are you here?

00:10:49.370 --> 00:10:53.750
Our schedules have been out of sync, so I wanted to take this opportunity to talk.

00:10:53.750 --> 00:10:56.510
When have we ever been in sync?

00:10:56.510 --> 00:10:58.470
See? It's because of that attitude!

00:10:58.470 --> 00:10:59.880
Mako-kun, you're so mean!

00:11:02.260 --> 00:11:03.510
Then, tell me-

00:11:03.510 --> 00:11:05.970
What is it? My three sizes are secret!

00:11:07.850 --> 00:11:10.980
How was Erio born?

00:11:11.770 --> 00:11:13.150
Did you know, Mako-kun...

00:11:13.150 --> 00:11:13.650
Yes?

00:11:13.650 --> 00:11:15.150
I'm not wearing a bra right now!

00:11:15.150 --> 00:11:17.610
That better lead to the answer to my question.

00:11:19.070 --> 00:11:22.360
There's nothing I can tell you.

00:11:22.360 --> 00:11:25.700
You see, I was having fun mixing everything in the drink bar,

00:11:25.700 --> 00:11:28.950
and I came up with a groovy juice!

00:11:28.950 --> 00:11:30.410
What?

00:11:30.410 --> 00:11:35.380
Conception resulting from an alien abduction is very much a theoretical possibility!

00:11:35.380 --> 00:11:37.670
It only means you were a party animal.

00:11:37.670 --> 00:11:38.260
Okay,

00:11:38.260 --> 00:11:39.210
I admit it.

00:11:39.210 --> 00:11:40.840
You're the father!

00:11:40.840 --> 00:11:41.340
Shut it.

00:11:41.340 --> 00:11:45.050
Honey, come here and play! Hurry!

00:11:45.050 --> 00:11:45.640
Shut up.

00:11:45.640 --> 00:11:48.140
There's nothing for you to play with.

00:11:48.140 --> 00:11:49.640
There's you.

00:11:50.980 --> 00:11:54.310
Let's play Old Maid.
I'm super good at it.

00:11:54.310 --> 00:11:56.190
We're really going to play?

00:11:57.440 --> 00:11:59.150
Let's bet something.

00:11:59.150 --> 00:12:02.360
If you win, I'll grant you any wish.

00:12:02.360 --> 00:12:04.280
What if I said I want a girl's panties?

00:12:04.280 --> 00:12:06.330
You're so bold!

00:12:06.330 --> 00:12:07.870
I said a <i>girl's</i>.

00:12:08.370 --> 00:12:11.710
You can just get as many as you want from the other room.

00:12:11.710 --> 00:12:12.790
Weird Mako-kun!

00:12:12.790 --> 00:12:14.750
Right, right, I'm weird!

00:12:14.750 --> 00:12:17.960
But I have to say, your brain is weirder!

00:12:17.960 --> 00:12:19.090
Here you go.

00:12:20.800 --> 00:12:22.010
DeLorean!

00:12:22.010 --> 00:12:24.260
Turn off your brain!

00:12:24.260 --> 00:12:26.850
What are you going to demand from me if you win?

00:12:26.850 --> 00:12:28.430
Let's see...

00:12:28.430 --> 00:12:29.970
Break up with your woman.

00:12:29.970 --> 00:12:33.100
I can't grant a wish beyond my powers!

00:12:33.730 --> 00:12:36.610
Yay! Meme-tan wins!

00:12:37.230 --> 00:12:39.480
13 straight losses... how?

00:12:39.480 --> 00:12:42.320
You agreed to use the cards I brought,

00:12:42.320 --> 00:12:45.110
and you let me shuffle and deal the cards.

00:12:45.110 --> 00:12:46.780
Those are the two reasons you lost.

00:12:46.780 --> 00:12:47.740
That's just cheating.

00:12:47.740 --> 00:12:51.540
Now, come here and we'll talk.

00:12:54.420 --> 00:12:55.620
So, what do you want to talk about?

00:13:03.260 --> 00:13:06.140
If you're after Erio for her looks,

00:13:06.140 --> 00:13:07.390
then back off.

00:13:14.770 --> 00:13:16.020
Mako-kun?

00:13:16.020 --> 00:13:18.480
Uh, you suddenly hugged me.

00:13:18.480 --> 00:13:21.360
Oh, I got you all excited.

00:13:23.740 --> 00:13:25.360
I'll say it again.

00:13:25.360 --> 00:13:29.160
If you're after Erio for her looks, then back off.

00:13:29.160 --> 00:13:32.620
You shouldn't carelessly befriend her.

00:13:32.620 --> 00:13:34.710
Did you come here just to tell me that?

00:13:34.710 --> 00:13:39.040
Yes, to tell you to leave her alone.

00:13:39.040 --> 00:13:40.880
I can't exactly do that.

00:13:40.880 --> 00:13:43.760
Why? There must be other girls that you're interested in.

00:13:43.760 --> 00:13:46.590
Or is she the only one?

00:13:46.590 --> 00:13:48.640
It's not affection or anything.

00:13:48.640 --> 00:13:51.260
Then why do you hang out with her?

00:13:51.260 --> 00:13:53.140
Out of curiosity.

00:13:53.140 --> 00:13:55.230
Also because I was dragged into it.

00:13:55.230 --> 00:13:57.140
She wants to be alone as much as possible,

00:13:57.140 --> 00:13:59.520
so all you have to do is respect her wish.

00:13:59.520 --> 00:14:02.150
Is that why you ignore her as much as possible?

00:14:02.150 --> 00:14:03.280
Yes.

00:14:03.730 --> 00:14:06.570
But you treasure her, don't you?

00:14:06.570 --> 00:14:09.450
That pod chair must have cost a fortune.

00:14:09.450 --> 00:14:13.080
Financial support alone is not enough to be a parent.

00:14:13.080 --> 00:14:15.790
I think you're a pretty good mother.

00:14:16.540 --> 00:14:22.540
A good mother would've been ready to raise her child when she was born.

00:14:23.800 --> 00:14:27.090
To be honest, I don't even remember when I conceived her.

00:14:27.090 --> 00:14:30.300
My memories of being pregnant are all pretty vague as well.

00:14:30.300 --> 00:14:34.390
Before I realized it, she was living in this house.

00:14:34.850 --> 00:14:38.100
Why did you hide her from our relatives?

00:14:38.100 --> 00:14:44.730
I didn't want people to badmouth her, calling her a bastard child.

00:14:46.650 --> 00:14:48.110
We're a little off-topic,

00:14:48.110 --> 00:14:52.280
but there's no need for you to burden yourself with her problems.

00:14:52.280 --> 00:14:54.540
Do we understand each other?

00:14:55.620 --> 00:14:57.370
I'll think about it later!

00:14:59.370 --> 00:15:01.000
Okay, let's sleep together!

00:15:01.000 --> 00:15:04.340
Go to sleep already. It's late.

00:15:04.880 --> 00:15:07.630
I thought you would be lonely by yourself.

00:15:07.630 --> 00:15:10.430
Aren't you the lonely one?

00:15:12.890 --> 00:15:14.010
Perhaps.

00:15:29.360 --> 00:15:30.900
It doesn't smell that mu-

00:15:30.900 --> 00:15:34.070
I didn't have my makeup on, so there won't be much smell left.

00:15:39.830 --> 00:15:41.830
You're going to scramble your brain.

00:15:42.420 --> 00:15:45.090
Did you teleport? I didn't hear your footsteps!

00:15:45.090 --> 00:15:48.840
I was hiding in Erio's room, so I could sneak back in to see you sleeping.

00:15:48.840 --> 00:15:51.220
Then I saw you... ah!

00:15:52.470 --> 00:15:55.470
Another memory that makes me want to kill myself.

00:15:55.470 --> 00:15:58.850
She's got leverage over me now.

00:16:03.230 --> 00:16:06.360
A normal, pretty girl until high school.

00:16:06.360 --> 00:16:08.190
Disappeared in June.

00:16:08.190 --> 00:16:10.240
She doesn't know why.

00:16:10.240 --> 00:16:13.240
She was floating in the sea half a year later, in November.

00:16:13.490 --> 00:16:16.740
She was unsettled about having no recollection of what happened.

00:16:16.740 --> 00:16:20.370
Blamed aliens for her amnesia as an escape from reality.

00:16:20.580 --> 00:16:25.290
Excess imagination caused her to declare she's an alien.

00:16:25.290 --> 00:16:27.540
Jumped off a bridge on a bike.

00:16:28.170 --> 00:16:30.800
Turned into a NEET who eats pizza in a strange way.

00:16:32.260 --> 00:16:36.930
Her straw of comfort is being sustained by her belief in aliens.

00:16:36.930 --> 00:16:39.720
That explanation is feasible enough.

00:16:39.720 --> 00:16:43.440
But she's not completely immersed in that illusion.

00:16:43.440 --> 00:16:44.480
On the other hand,

00:16:44.480 --> 00:16:46.690
there's nothing that can be done about her memory.

00:16:46.690 --> 00:16:51.820
If she can't remember it herself, I surely can't help her.

00:16:51.820 --> 00:16:56.780
Breaking her belief is the only thing within the reach of this hand.

00:16:57.530 --> 00:16:59.620
I'll break that illusion of yours!

00:16:59.620 --> 00:17:00.700
No, no.

00:17:00.700 --> 00:17:03.250
I'm not such a hot-headed character.

00:17:03.830 --> 00:17:06.750
Meme-san told me to not to be superficial...

00:17:07.540 --> 00:17:10.090
which is exactly what I've been doing.

00:17:10.090 --> 00:17:16.260
This is definitely one of those rare occasions where an adult's advice should be heeded.

00:17:16.260 --> 00:17:18.760
The rational side of me is saying the same thing.

00:17:18.760 --> 00:17:23.140
However, in reality, I'm involved with Erio, and I'm thinking about her.

00:17:23.140 --> 00:17:24.350
She claims to be an alien,

00:17:24.350 --> 00:17:25.690
she claims to be able to fly,

00:17:25.690 --> 00:17:27.350
she claims to be evaluating Earthlings,

00:17:27.350 --> 00:17:30.770
but Touwa Erio can't really prove any of the above.

00:17:30.770 --> 00:17:31.900
I don't like it.

00:17:31.900 --> 00:17:35.150
I can't stand the fact that she believes in aliens for pessimistic reasons.

00:17:36.150 --> 00:17:38.530
Mystical things should be filled with hope.

00:17:38.820 --> 00:17:40.620
Like the way I dream of unknown creatures in the deep sea,

00:17:40.620 --> 00:17:46.000
it should be an existence that keeps pushing one forward.

00:17:46.790 --> 00:17:48.790
Yet Touwa Erio anchored it to her past,

00:17:48.790 --> 00:17:52.920
letting it serve only as a reassurance of her lost time.

00:17:52.920 --> 00:17:54.550
She's a failure of a human being.

00:17:55.260 --> 00:17:58.050
Still, she's not an alien.

00:17:58.050 --> 00:18:00.800
That's why, <i>that's why</i>...

00:18:00.800 --> 00:18:02.930
I don't care about what happens in the future.

00:18:02.930 --> 00:18:03.680
But...

00:18:04.180 --> 00:18:07.690
I'll resolve what bothers me right now!

00:18:07.690 --> 00:18:09.270
Okay, okay, okay...

00:18:09.270 --> 00:18:10.440
Okay!

00:18:20.120 --> 00:18:22.080
I'll fly in the sky with you.

00:18:22.080 --> 00:18:24.580
If you fail, you're becoming an Earthling.

00:18:27.540 --> 00:18:29.080
I just remembered...

00:18:29.080 --> 00:18:32.710
this bicycle is the same model they used in the film <i>E.T.</i>

00:18:32.710 --> 00:18:37.550
I don't believe for a second this thing is going to fly, though.

00:18:38.010 --> 00:18:41.430
Not for others, but to force my belief onto others.

00:18:41.430 --> 00:18:44.140
It's such a selfish flight.

00:18:44.140 --> 00:18:46.430
I definitely won't let her use faulty equipment as an excuse.

00:18:46.430 --> 00:18:50.060
Let's have the Earth's gravity crush her straight.

00:18:50.060 --> 00:18:51.560
Hey, E.T.

00:18:51.560 --> 00:18:52.770
Get in the basket.

00:18:52.770 --> 00:18:54.320
Wouldn't that put you in the mood to fly?

00:18:55.820 --> 00:18:58.030
You can return to outer space if you can fly.

00:18:58.030 --> 00:18:58.820
Straight out.

00:19:01.950 --> 00:19:04.030
Still slow after maintenance.

00:19:14.040 --> 00:19:16.710
We'll speed down the hill toward the cliff,

00:19:16.710 --> 00:19:19.670
and decelerate immediately after Erio panics from fear.

00:19:19.670 --> 00:19:24.300
Then we'll adjust trajectory, touchdown, and I'll issue her an Earthling citizenship card.

00:19:24.760 --> 00:19:26.770
This is a chicken race...

00:19:26.770 --> 00:19:29.100
until she chickens out.

00:19:32.150 --> 00:19:33.400
So heavy!

00:19:37.530 --> 00:19:38.490
Wait a minute.

00:19:38.490 --> 00:19:40.280
I really can't stop from this speed.

00:19:40.280 --> 00:19:42.280
The brakes aren't working!

00:19:44.030 --> 00:19:45.740
We're definitely dead if I veer off-course.

00:19:45.740 --> 00:19:46.990
How do I stop? Should I use my feet?

00:19:46.990 --> 00:19:48.750
I'll have to. This isn't good!

00:19:48.750 --> 00:19:52.370
There goes my shoe! No sign of stopping!

00:19:52.370 --> 00:19:54.380
Downhill is scary, more so than sweet rice cakes!

00:19:54.380 --> 00:19:55.710
I can only pray!

00:19:55.710 --> 00:19:59.170
Stop, stop, stop, stop...

00:19:59.170 --> 00:20:00.420
I'm Makoto.

00:20:00.420 --> 00:20:01.260
Stop it.

00:20:01.260 --> 00:20:02.300
Make time stop!

00:20:02.300 --> 00:20:05.140
Stop, stop, stop, stop!

00:20:05.140 --> 00:20:07.010
N-No, right.

00:20:07.010 --> 00:20:09.310
Fly? The sea? The guard rail!

00:20:11.810 --> 00:20:13.560
Damn, damn, damn, damn!

00:20:13.980 --> 00:20:17.070
Damn it, just go for it!

00:20:19.070 --> 00:20:25.320
<i>I can't fly!</i>

00:20:31.710 --> 00:20:34.420
We're flying!

00:20:34.420 --> 00:20:35.080
We're still...

00:20:39.210 --> 00:20:40.920
We're falling!

00:20:59.820 --> 00:21:00.780
Why?

00:21:00.780 --> 00:21:03.650
I'm an alien, so I should be able to fly.

00:21:03.650 --> 00:21:05.320
No, we definitely flew!

00:21:05.320 --> 00:21:05.950
A little.

00:21:05.950 --> 00:21:06.700
Three miles.

00:21:06.700 --> 00:21:07.490
Ah!

00:21:07.490 --> 00:21:09.280
But do I have to admit it?

00:21:09.280 --> 00:21:11.370
Am I an Earthling? Why?

00:21:11.370 --> 00:21:12.500
Well, I kind of know why.

00:21:12.500 --> 00:21:13.160
No, I don't!

00:21:13.160 --> 00:21:14.500
"Serves you right!"

00:21:14.500 --> 00:21:18.000
would make me an instant villain.

00:21:18.000 --> 00:21:19.340
Fake alien!

00:21:19.340 --> 00:21:21.050
How does the Earth's salt water taste?

00:21:21.050 --> 00:21:24.420
It's not properly seasoned and the service is poor.

00:21:24.420 --> 00:21:26.430
You failed miserably.

00:21:26.430 --> 00:21:29.390
Outer space is nothing. We didn't even reach Enoshima!

00:21:29.390 --> 00:21:33.430
My secretary did it. I'm not involved in any shape, way or form.

00:21:33.430 --> 00:21:37.730
You still failed, and I don't mind being the principle offender.

00:21:38.730 --> 00:21:40.730
What was the purpose of this?

00:21:40.730 --> 00:21:42.980
Is a purpose or an incentive even necessary?

00:21:42.980 --> 00:21:43.610
Of course-

00:21:48.740 --> 00:21:49.950
Let's get along!

00:21:49.950 --> 00:21:50.490
Huh?

00:21:50.490 --> 00:21:52.370
That's the human ideal.

00:21:52.370 --> 00:21:55.000
Just aim for that and you'll be fine.

00:21:55.000 --> 00:21:56.370
Sounds fishy to me.

00:21:56.830 --> 00:21:59.670
Get along? You really hurt me!

00:21:59.670 --> 00:22:02.210
My identity was destroyed and now I'm freezing.

00:22:02.210 --> 00:22:05.590
The cousin's victorious smirk is a violation of intergalactic law, too!

00:22:05.590 --> 00:22:10.350
No relationship ever ends peacefully without someone getting hurt.

00:22:10.350 --> 00:22:11.600
He's not even making any sense.

00:22:11.600 --> 00:22:13.520
Actually, there was no relationship to begin with.

00:22:13.520 --> 00:22:15.230
This is the first time we've met.

00:22:15.230 --> 00:22:18.520
I want to get along with the girl who just returned to Earth.

00:22:18.520 --> 00:22:21.270
If you're suffering or distressed from non-existent memories,

00:22:21.270 --> 00:22:23.280
I want to at least listen to you complain.

00:22:23.820 --> 00:22:25.780
That's why we're here today. For recreation.

00:22:27.530 --> 00:22:31.120
To get along, we have to know each other first.

00:22:31.120 --> 00:22:32.950
In other words, self introduction is important-

00:22:32.950 --> 00:22:34.540
I-I'm...

00:22:34.950 --> 00:22:37.250
Hey, I'm not finished yet!

00:22:43.210 --> 00:22:45.840
Hey, Earthling. Identify yourself!

00:22:50.090 --> 00:22:51.600
Touwa Erio.

00:22:51.600 --> 00:22:54.970
All right, I'm Niwa Makoto. Nice to meet you!

00:24:32.820 --> 00:24:34.820
The cousin's current assessment:

00:24:34.820 --> 00:24:37.200
First date with Ryuushi-san: +3

00:24:37.200 --> 00:24:40.080
My aunt stole my first hug: -5

00:24:40.080 --> 00:24:42.750
Sneaked out of school: +2

00:24:42.750 --> 00:24:45.460
I cannot fly: +5

00:24:45.460 --> 00:24:49.050
Current adolescence points total: +1

00:24:49.050 --> 00:24:53.800
Crossing the boundary of trauma and glory,
disappeared, and hospitalized.

00:24:54.300 --> 00:24:57.600
Next time: Broken Right Arm, a Month to Recover.

00:24:57.600 --> 00:25:00.680
If it's a hospital, there must be nurses! Not eggplants!
